Current Dev Position: YP 2.5 M1 development

Next Deadline: YP 2.5 M1 cut off of 12/4/17


SWAT team rotation: Paul -> Todor on Nov. 24, 2017.

SWAT team rotation: Todor -> Tracy on Dec. 1, 2017.

https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Yocto_Build_Failure_Swat_Team


Key Status/Updates:

=B7        We are continuing to suffer intermittent build failures and are =
continuing to attempt to debug these.

=B7        One piece of good news is that the qemuppc issue has been tracke=
d down to a bug in qemu and we have a patch merged to address that.

=B7        Sadly:

o   The 4.3.12 kernel did not resolve the tumbleweed/f26 qemu hangs. It doe=
s appears to be a KVM APIC virtualization problem limited to mmio. If we en=
able x2apic which mostly uses msr accesses, the problem is significantly re=
duced.

o   We also have a hang issue with morty builds, occurring in smart through=
 rpm/libdb with a mutex/pthread lockup. We don=92t know why morty has start=
ed showing this issue on all builds, it is blocking the point release.

=B7        Until we resolve these issues patches will continue to be slow t=
o merge, if at all. This also blocks several core developers from doing any=
 feature work at this point in time (e.g. layer setup tool is on hold, agai=
n).

=B7        We can only continue to stress that unless others step up and he=
lp to try and root cause these issues, things will stall with the project.


Planned upcoming dot releases:

YP 2.2.3 is planned and should be out in the next few weeks when the hang i=
ssue is solved.

YP 2.3.3 is planned, but date TBD during YP 2.5 planning.

YP 2.4.1 is planned, but date TBD during YP 2.5 planning.


Key YP 2.5 Dates are:

YP 2.5 M1 cut off of 12/4/17

